# Without this file, `COPY . .` pulls the local 1.4GB .venv into the image —
# on top of the dependencies pip already installed. It built and ran fine and
# was simply 1.4GB larger than it needed to be, which is exactly the kind of
# waste nobody notices until the deploy is slow.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.git/
.gitignore
.claude/

# Runtime state. The image seeds its own index at build time from
# data/eval_corpus/, so shipping a local index would just be overwritten —
# and would bake whatever happened to be on the dev machine into the image.
data/chroma/
data/lesson4_chroma/
data/chunks.json
data/uploads/
data/eval_results.json

.DS_Store
*.md
!README.md
